/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*--------------------------------*\
  species/NH2COO.dat -- the CARBAMATE ion, CASE-LOCAL.

  The carbamate is the species that makes an ammonia-rich carbonated water
  different from a carbonate water: at Table 7's conditions it holds a
  substantial share of the dissolved CO2, and a network without it reports
  molecular molalities the paper's own predictions contradict.  It enters the
  catalogue here, beside the one case that exercises it, rather than in
  data/standards/ -- promotion of a species record is a curation act, and the
  standards tree is not edited as a side effect of building an anchor case.

  Identity only: no aqueousThermo block, because Edwards (1978) publishes the
  equilibrium (Eq 20), not a formation enthalpy on the elements datum, and an
  absent datum must keep meaning absent (any energy path that needs it will
  refuse by name, which is correct).
\*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
recordType modelSpecies;
schemaVersion 1;

name    NH2COO;
formula     "NH2COO-";
charge  -1;
MW { value 60.032; unit g/mol;}   // N 14.007 + H2 2.016 + C 12.011 + O2 31.998
